It does seem like Postgres hard caps at 24 hours though.
```
postgres=# select CAST('24:00:00' AS time);
   time   
----------
 24:00:00
(1 row)

postgres=# select CAST('36:00:00' AS time);
ERROR:  date/time field value out of range: "36:00:00"
LINE 1: select CAST('36:00:00' AS time);
                    ^
postgres=# select CAST('24:00:01' AS time);
ERROR:  date/time field value out of range: "24:00:01"
LINE 1: select CAST('24:00:01' AS time);
```

Does that mean we need to actively check scanned time values from Arrow to see if they break our accepted bounds?
